  "scope": "# Prepare a bounded native check of lean next-token training\n\nThe completed CPU check shows that deleting the zero-weight auxiliary head\npreserves the checked prediction loss, gradients and first optimizer update.\nIt removes 24,608,000 unused training parameters. This alone does not qualify\nnative headless training or justify repricing any completed model history.\n\nPrepare a separate numerical check while the fixed-control replication runs.\nUse zero accelerator chips during preparation. Change no frozen source or\nworker in that campaign. This preparation does not admit a native job.\n\nReuse the existing complete lean Parcae qualification trainer and independent\npinned-upstream checker, with an explicit wrapper selecting the already checked\nFP32 primitive-attention body and runtime-scalar optimizer. Keep FP16 body,\nFP32 vocabulary head/masters/moments, manual loss scale 8192, global 512 natural\nwindows, accumulation 16, and the same 2/2/2 model. The auxiliary projection,\nloss and parameter inventory are absent. Count the real next-token projection,\nattention, full backward and all 32 replicated optimizer matrix updates.\n\nTwo qualification cases execute deterministic depths one and two, with full\ngradients. The old worker's CLI selectors are `fixed1` and `poisson2`; the latter\nis only a legacy selector here. Its prepared table is uniformly (2, 2), never a\nPoisson sample. Preserve that distinction in all public summaries.\n\nUse the original qualification-only seed-1009 initializer, not a trained\ncheckpoint. The new preparation references its immutable existing file, and\nthe independent CPU auditor uses that very same initializer. Both bodies have\n141,963,840 parameters. Qualification states remain ineligible for science.\n\nA future warm phase performs 121 updates, measuring exactly updates 21\u2013120;\na separate fresh-process replay performs update 121 from the full update-120\ncheckpoint. The existing changing qualification schedule peaks at 1e-4, with\nthe same first-update schedule as the original independent optimizer checker.\nThis is a conservative numerical/throughput schedule, not LR selection or\nevidence that 1e-4 is a good scientific learning rate. The runtime-scalar\noptimizer has already been checked at the scientific selected rates separately.\n\nBefore a scientific lean fit, require complete global gradients against CPU\nFP32, the independent first optimizer-step check, all-replica equality, exact\nloaded optimizer/model/RNG state and the registered 2% update/moment replay\ncriterion. Report bit equality separately; do not promise identical future\ntrajectories. Require actual 100-update timings and a separately measured\nscientific budget. No new operators or numerical tolerances are introduced.\n\nAt preparation, check exact original source, initializer and corpus identities,\nboth fixed-depth tables and exact work ledgers. The existing CPU parity receipt\nis a prerequisite, not a new result produced by metadata preparation. The\nlegacy-compatible CPU marker records this inheritance explicitly.\n\nDo not launch native qualification while the current main comparison owns the\ninstance. Before its outcomes, declare that the lean follow-up is warranted only\nif both seed-specific recurrent gains are positive against each work control\nand both two-seed mean gains are at least 0.01 nats. Otherwise retain the lean\npreparation without native expenditure. This is a DEV resource-allocation gate,\nnot confirmation or a change to the running experiment's analysis.\n\nAny eventual qualification admission needs its own fixed one-hour cap, phase\nbounds, complete costs and at least 65 GiB NVMe free in addition to the usual\n512 GiB available-memory / 35 GiB filesystem / 10,000-inode guards. Preserve\nfailed and stopped work. No learned state, held-out quality result, TEST access,\nreserve access, terminal alpha or large fit is authorized by this preparation.\n",
